From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mali_kbase: cast VM_NORESERVE to typed vma_flags_t for shmem_file_setup()

Kernel 7.2 gave VMA flags a distinct type-safe `vma_flags_t` (struct
wrapping a bitmap; see include/linux/mm_types.h) instead of a plain
unsigned long, and shmem_file_setup()'s third parameter is now
`vma_flags_t flags` (include/linux/shmem_fs.h). The legacy
VM_NORESERVE macro still exists for back-compat call sites that want
the old-style unsigned long bitmask (it expands through
INIT_VM_FLAG()/BIT() to `long unsigned int`), but passing it directly
where a `vma_flags_t` is expected is now a real type mismatch, not
just a style issue -- confirmed by the compiler error citing
"expected 'vma_flags_t' but argument is of type 'long unsigned int'".

Fix: use mk_vma_flags(VMA_NORESERVE_BIT), the typed constructor for
exactly this bit. This is not a new idiom invented for this driver --
it's the same pattern this kernel's own mm/memfd.c already uses for
an identical shmem_file_setup(..., mk_vma_flags(VMA_NORESERVE_BIT))
call, confirmed by reading that call site directly. Both symbols
(mk_vma_flags, VMA_NORESERVE_BIT) are declared in include/linux/mm.h,
which was already transitively visible here (the file already
compiled VM_NORESERVE from the same header before this change).

Two call sites in mali_kbase_csf.c (kbase_csf_scheduler_group_get_db /
the CSF doorbell mmap and the CSF user_reg mmap setup), both passing
VM_NORESERVE to shmem_file_setup() the same way.

Fixes the mali_kbase.ko build against kernel 7.2.0-rc4-sky1-ncz (found
in the same build pass as patch 0012, both were the next errors after
0008-0011 unblocked earlier translation units).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c	2026-07-26 03:23:18.857683691 +0800
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/csf/mali_kbase_csf.c	2026-07-26 03:23:18.876750721 +0800
@@ -3769,7 +3769,7 @@
 	struct file *filp;
 	int ret;
 
-	filp = shmem_file_setup("mali csf db", MAX_LFS_FILESIZE, VM_NORESERVE);
+	filp = shmem_file_setup("mali csf db", MAX_LFS_FILESIZE, mk_vma_flags(VMA_NORESERVE_BIT));
 	if (IS_ERR(filp))
 		return PTR_ERR(filp);
 
@@ -3835,7 +3835,7 @@
 
 	kbdev->csf.user_reg.filp = NULL;
 
-	filp = shmem_file_setup("mali csf user_reg", MAX_LFS_FILESIZE, VM_NORESERVE);
+	filp = shmem_file_setup("mali csf user_reg", MAX_LFS_FILESIZE, mk_vma_flags(VMA_NORESERVE_BIT));
 	if (IS_ERR(filp)) {
 		dev_err(kbdev->dev, "failed to get an unlinked file for user_reg");
 		return PTR_ERR(filp);
